# Three-man positions for the differential Syzygy gate.
#
# `cargo xtask tb` drives rfish and a pristine upstream build over each of these and
# compares the WDL verdict and the DTZ distance.
#
# Every entry is LEGAL. An illegal one -- where the side not to move is in check -- makes
# the oracle exit rather than answer, which reads to a gate as a broken engine rather than
# as a position to skip. The generator's own filter missed several, so the list was sieved
# by feeding it through rfish and keeping what its FEN parser accepted.
#
# The battery covers every table (KQvK, KRvK, KBvK, KNvK, KPvK), both colours to move, and
# the four cases the index computation folds differently: the corner, the edge, the centre
# and the long a1-h8 diagonal. It also covers the two paths that are easy to get wrong and
# that no single position exercises:
#
#   - BLACK STRONGER. A file stores KRvK and never KvKR, so a position where the lone king
#     is White has to be mirrored before the lookup. Positions below with the piece on the
#     black side reach it.
#   - CHANGE_STM. A DTZ file stores one side to move only. When the probe wants the other,
#     the answer comes from a one-ply search that minimises the distance, not from the file.

4k3/8/8/8/8/8/8/Q3K3 w - - 0 1
4k3/8/8/8/8/5Q2/8/4K3 w - - 0 1
8/8/8/8/8/8/8/2Q1K2k w - - 0 1
